From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Douglas Panhota <douglaspands@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: phy: rockchip,inno-usb2phy: add rockchip,vbus-always-on

Some boards do not route VBUS of the OTG connector to the PHY, so the
B-session valid signal never rises (the R36S V5 handheld, RK3326). The
OTG state machine then powers the port off on its first run and never
powers it on again for a device role. Describe such a port with a
boolean, the same name the Rockchip BSP kernel uses.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/rockchip,inno-usb2phy.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/rockchip,inno-usb2phy.yaml
index 58e735b..9e9e43c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/rockchip,inno-usb2phy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/rockchip,inno-usb2phy.yaml
@@ -129,6 +129,14 @@ properties:
           Phandle to a regulator that provides power to VBUS.
           See ./phy-bindings.txt for details.

+      rockchip,vbus-always-on:
+        type: boolean
+        description:
+          The board does not route VBUS of this connector to the PHY. The
+          B-session valid signal is ignored and the port is never powered
+          off for lack of VBUS; the controller decides the role (from the ID
+          pin or a USB role switch that overrides the session signals).
+
     required:
       - "#phy-cells"

